#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
A Interaction Metrics Analyzer (v3)
======================================

M1 problems | M2 intents/sub-intents | M3 workflows + tools per workflow
M4 workflow reuse vs new-every-run | M5 A API agent/tool side + parallel
M6 baseline volume, +ve vs -ve

Standard library only. Nothing about the schema is hardcoded: field names,
namespaces and thresholds are all patterns or CLI flags.

v3 fixes
--------
P1  Problem text no longer harvested from inside tool payloads (v2 returned
    values like "300GB" / "PRICE_PLAN" scraped out of tool responses).
P2  Tool names canonicalised from the data itself: if both "get_pgw_hlr" and
    "nsm-get_pgw_hlr" appear, they are recognised as one tool. Alias map is
    reported, never assumed.
P3  Tool coverage added: what share of interactions call each tool. Separates
    "always-on" tools from intent-driven ones.
P4  Workflow clustering switched from transitive union-find (which chained
    everything into mega-clusters) to non-transitive leader clustering, plus a
    built-in sensitivity sweep so the cluster count is never quoted blind.
P5  Timestamps validated against a plausibility window; the key that produced
    each timestamp is reported so the real event-time field can be identified.
P6  Cluster exports now carry interaction counts (v2 left them blank).

Usage
-----
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py interactions.csv
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py "C:/path/output_1998_complete_interactions"
    python A_metrics_analyzer.py interactions.csv --start-date 2026-06-01 \
        --end-date 2026-08-31 --output-dir ./metrics_aug
"""
